## 5. Confirmed Design Decisions

> [!NOTE]
> The following decisions have been confirmed by the user:

1. **Packaging & Dependency Management**: Using `pip` + `requirements.txt` with `pyyaml>=6.0.1` and `python-dotenv>=1.0.1`.
2. **Class & Task Naming**: 1:1 match to Ruby: `boukensha.tasks.Base` and `boukensha.tasks.Player`, `boukensha.Config`.
3. **Settings File Extension**: Specifically checking `settings.yml` (matching Ruby's `config.rb`).
4. **Prompt File Location**: Copying `prompts/system.md` into `week1_baseline/python/00_config/prompts/system.md` to keep the Python component standalone.
5. **Runner Script**: Creating [week1_baseline/bin/00_config_py.sh](file:///Users/vivekmitra/Desktop/Learn2Code/Anthropic/claude-code-camp-2026-Q2/week1_baseline/bin/00_config_py.sh) alongside [week1_baseline/bin/00_config.sh](file:///Users/vivekmitra/Desktop/Learn2Code/Anthropic/claude-code-camp-2026-Q2/week1_baseline/bin/00_config.sh).

